                "quote": "do! ensure (not (library.Members.ContainsKey memberId)) (DuplicateMember memberId)"
              }
            ],
            "rationale": "The rule that member ids are unique is written again inside restoreMember instead of reusing the existing check in Catalog.addMember. I infer that addMember has the same check from the matching pattern in addBook and from the shared DuplicateMember error, which gives the expected 'member m1 already exists' message. Both copies are in Tier 2 and they agree, but there are now two places that can drift apart. Everything else uses a single definition: loadBackup for the missing-backup error and commit for persisting state.",
